ly under equipped and  underprepared hero raced a few blocks  over to find the source from a distance  all he could see was a man fumbling with  the door of a locked car clearly unable  to open it and trying to force his way  in what this so-called hero didn't think  to do was assess the situation for any  further context too quick to trust in  his instincts  he declared unable to hear how muffled  his voice sounded when filtered through  the material of the ski mask the man  froze and turned to look at the figure  approaching him only to raise an eyebrow  in confusion ah hello he called back can  I help you silence villain the Mast  onlooker shouted just oddly over the  noisy Car Alarm we've got two choices  here either you walk away leave that  person's property alone and I'll let you  off with a warning or we do this the  hard way and you'll face Zach paused for  dramatic effect like he practiced in the  mirror but Wrath of Captain Katana of  who the other man replied look man I'm  not sure what your deal is if this is  some kind of cosplay thing or you're  just nuts but this is my car okay the  door gets stuck I just need to Jimmy it  a little sometimes but it sets the alarm  off wire Captain Katana yelled reaching  over his shoulder his gloved hand  gripped the hilt of his weapon and  pulled it free of its sheath from across  the parking lot the driver couldn't tell  how utterly useless the sword was at his  current distance all he saw was amassed  potentially unhinged stranger  dramatically pacing towards him with  what was very clearly a weapon what the  hell he exclaimed urgently trying to get  his car door open the handle gave way  and the door sprung open allowing the  man to hurriedly climb into the driver's  seat and shut the door behind him  starting the engine the lights came on  and illuminated The Stranger in front of  him who stood looking absolutely  ridiculous in his outfit consisting of  what looked like various pieces of  sportswear Katana and hand the superhero  was still striding slowly towards the  car as the engine spluttered into life  Zack stopped smiling under the material  of his hockey  as he gripped both hands around the hilt  and took a wide stance flooring the  accelerator the driver was eager to get  away from the obvious lunatic even if he  was wielding a sword that was mostly  unusable it didn't seem like that would  stop Captain Katana from trying to use  it no matter how unsuccessfully the car  came barreling towards Zach and he  readied himself lifting the blade high  above his head he knew that he would be  able to bring it downwards in a  Victorious swipe at precisely the right  moment the second the worn out dulled  metal connected with that of the car it  would slice the stolen vehicle into two  perfect pieces split right down the  middle leaving the thief confounded and  ready to be handed over to police you  can already guess that's not what  happened can you with barely a screech  of tires against the concrete and  without even enough distance to build up  that much speed the car headed straight  for Captain Katana he made a flailing  uncoordinated swing far too early  causing the sword to bounce right off  the hood of the car the force of the  impact wasn't huge but it was enough to  cause the katana to slip from the  wannabe Hero's hands helped by the fact  his gloves didn't have that much grip on  them the katana of apparent  invincibility was sent sailing through  the air and came clattering to the  ground rolling under another car in the  parking lot although Zach was a little  preoccupied to see where it landed no  sooner had he lost his grip on his  Almighty weapon of Justice around three  and a half thousand pounds of metal  collided with Captain Katana felled on  his first ever night as a superhero by  his very first villain still Zach at  least learned what his Kryptonite was  his greatest weakness just like so many  classic superheroes had his just  happened to be being hit by a midsize  sedan tumbling back onto the ground the  back of Captain katana's head thumped  heavily against the cold hard concrete  leaving him with a concussion and an  overwhelming sense of embarrassment as  the driver parked his car and called an  ambulance at least he now knew he never  wanted to pick up that sword  you see that's the second remarkable  thing about  scp-572 anyone who picks it up instantly  perceives it as a mighty weapon the kind  you would find in an ancient legend  despite the sword being crudely made  blunt and generally unfit for any use  the wielder will maintain the belief  that it not only has perfect balance and  cutting power but that the sword has  also imbued them with unparalleled  strength and invincibility to damage  it's all a delusion of course and  whoever holds that sword will gladly  prove it to you they'll try to perform  incredibly risky stunts with it only to  end up severely injuring themselves in  the process don't worry though if you  ever come across scp-572 it's nothing a  quick thump in the back of the head  won't fix now if you want to hear about  an actual all-powerful sword that can  obliterate anything on an atomic level  as well as the ancient energy being who  wields it then you should go and check  out scp-001 the gate guardian and of  course sometimes the only thing better  than one Katana is two tanas and an  Infamous comic book character but will  that be enough to take on the hard to  destroy reptile find out in Deadpool  versus scp-682
 

